{
  "kind": "tea",
  "teaId": "widow-mite",
  "text": "He sat down and watched people give, and the one he pointed at had less than everybody.\n\nMark twelve. And the setup is the part people skip. \"Jesus sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury.\"\n\nHe sat down. And watched. On purpose.\n\nAnd many that were rich cast in much. That's in the text too. It's not a lie, they gave a lot.\n\nThen a certain poor widow comes and throws in two mites. And Mark actually converts the currency for his readers, which tells you how small it was. Two mites, which make a farthing.\n\nAnd Jesus calls his disciples over. He wants them to see this specifically.\n\n\"Verily I say unto you, that this poor widow hath cast more in, than all they which have cast into the treasury.\"\n\nMore than all of them. Combined.\n\nAnd then he does the maths out loud. \"For all they did cast in of their abundance. But she of her want did cast in all that she had, even all her living.\"\n\nAll her living. Not a percentage. Everything.\n\nHe is not measuring the gift. He is measuring what was left afterwards.",
